INVALID RUN -- do not cite as a guard observation.
The kernel under test (sha256 3a63fe94...) carried the first version of the
block-boundary stop, which treated any VAR_BLK<>0 source as a 1KB block
buffer. Boot-time embedded-vocab evaluation sets VAR_BLK=1 as a "not
interactive" flag over a multi-KB continuous stream (forth.asm cold_start),
so every compile-mode string past offset 1024 truncated and TOIN was
clamped mid-string: the interpreter was dead before the first probe.
Nothing in this log observes the in-loop DICT_LIMIT guard. Root cause and
fix (source-identity cap, VAR_STR_CAP) recorded in the commit that
supersedes this run. Preserved per the run-1 precedent: invalid artifacts
are kept, not deleted.

